ctures and distributes paints, coatings, and specialty materials in the United States, Canada, the Asia Pacific, Latin America, Europe, the Middle East, and Africa. It operates through three segments: Global Architectural Coatings, Performance Coatings, and Industrial Coatings. The Global Architectural Coatings segment supplies a variety of decorative coatings, adhesives, sealants, and finishes, as well as paint strippers, stains, and related chemicals. Its Performance Coatings segment offers aerospace coatings, automotive refinishing coatings, protective and marine coatings, and traffic solutions comprising paints, thermoplastics, raised pavement markers, and other technologies for pavement marking. The Industrial Coatings segment provides automotive OEM coatings, industrial coatings, and packaging coatings, as well as specialty products, such as optical monomers and coatings, low-friction coatings, and other specialty products. The company delivers its products to company-owned stores, home centers and other consumer retail outlets, paint dealers, concessionaires and independent distributors, company-owned distribution networks, and directly to manufacturing companies and retail customers. PPG Industries, Inc. was incorporated in 1883 and is headquartered in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Timothy M. Knavish | CEO & Chairman | Age 59 | Compensation: $3.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 43K people. Revenue per employee of $365K ranks in the bottom quartile among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $27K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["PPG Industries, Inc. is a large-cap basic materials business with a $25.9B market cap on $15.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +0% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 9% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 2.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 8.5\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 49% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.49232849728069983},{"text":"Basic Materials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Basic Materials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 13% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","42 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PPG named to TIME Magazine\u2019s \u2018America\u2019s Top Manufacturers 2027\u2019 list","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ppg-named-time-magazine-america-130000716.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795179600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Are Wall Street Analysts Predicting PPG Industries Stock Will Climb or Sink?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/wall-street-analysts-predicting-ppg-123944823.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795178384.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(PPG) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/14/PPG_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_111926091202_1795097522.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795097522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"PPG inducts six new members into Collegium association","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/articles/ppg-inducts-six-members-collegium-130300449.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795093380.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentim